    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `householdId` is now a deterministic function of `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`, and everything that keys off the household uses that computed id.\n\n**`HouseholdIdGenerator`** \u2014 changed the key from `normalize(lastName) + \"\\n\" + normalize(address)` to `normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode` (first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256), with `null` postcode contributing an empty component. Updated the signature to `generate(lastName, postcode)` and the javadoc.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`**\n- Computes and sets `householdId` **up front for every owner** (so `sharesHousehold` no longer \"creates the link\" \u2014 it's automatic).\n- After finding household members (owners sharing the computed `householdId`), if any exist and `sharesHousehold` is not set, it throws the new **`HouseholdDuplicateException`** (409). With `sharesHousehold`, the owner is created as a declared member.\n- Removed the old `joinHousehold` method (the link is now deterministic).\n- `householdSize` is computed from `findHouseholdMembers`, which now keys off the computed `householdId` instead of last-name+address.\n\n**`findHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 now matches existing owners whose recomputed `householdId` equals the new owner's (robust to owners/seed rows with a stale/null stored value); an owner with no postcode has no household peers.\n\n**`flagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 now takes the household members and the `sharesHousehold` flag: a declared member is never flagged as a suspected duplicate (`possibleDuplicate=false`); otherwise it soft-matches a household member with a different telephone.\n\n**`HouseholdDuplicateException`** (new) + a handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** returning 409 Conflict.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions to the new `(lastName, postcode)` semantics.\n\n`rejectIdentityCollision` is unchanged but now sees the always-populated `householdId` via the identity key, so identity-collision detection also keys off the computed household as required.\n\nBuild: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: the spec makes any second owner in a household a 409 (unless `sharesHousehold`), which is broader than the old soft-match. As a result, the only reachable path where `flagPossibleDuplicate` runs against a non-empty household is the declared-member path \u2014 where the spec requires `possibleDuplicate=false`. I kept the method's soft-match logic intact anyway so the behavior stays correct and self-documenting rather than hard-coding `false`. I also chose to treat a `null` postcode as \"no household\" (mirroring the prior \"no postcode can't match\" philosophy) so postcode-less owners aren't blocked; the deterministic id is still always set.",
